A few things - jumping always takes one turn (not one move), so expert
jumping with very fast won't be any faster than expert jumping at base
speed. Also, unskilled jumping (or boots) are fine to get across
Medusa. On Astral, the candelabrum is a great option, since it has a
radius of 4, allowing you to use expert jumping fully, even in dark
rooms (and with expert jumping, you shouldn't really be on Astral long
enough for the candelabrum to burn out).

